<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean Kia Motors 1996 net falls.</title>
<headline>S.Korean Kia Motors 1996 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31</p>
<p>(in billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (won)			     93    vs 155</p>
<p>    Net					7.04 vs  11.48</p>
<p>    Dividend (pct)			 none vs   1.5 in stocks</p>
<p>    Turnover			   6,607.14 vs 5,688.54</p>
<p>    Profit before tax		   12.92 vs    11.59</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	     0.95 (loss) vs     1.81 (gain)</p>
<p>NOTE - Kia Motors Corp is South Korea's second-largest car maker. Its share capital increased by 1.11 million shares to 75.63 million in 1996 due to dividend payments in stocks.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5646</p>
</text>
